            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For reference the Microsoft link where they describe this is https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-language/maximum-string-length?view=msvc-170. Obviously all compilers have some limits somewhere though so it isn't exclusive to Microsoft (although GCC and clang tend to be a bit bigger I think)\n\n> If the target compiler genuinely can't represent the constant, I'd expect the build to fail with an error rather than produce a silently corrupted extension.\n\nI'd claim that this bit of it *really* should be on Microsoft since it's much easier for them to detect that they've failed than for us to. So please do complain to them! \n\nI agree that it's probably worth trying to avoid the issue in Cython if there's a sensible way of doing so though.\n",
