            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Additional thoughts: on more recent Cython versions we've changed how strings are loaded. That makes it both better and worse: \n* All the strings are now concatenated into a single C string. That makes it worse because you're more likely to hit the limit. \n* The strings are now compressed (and decompressed to convert them to Python strings). Obviously your example compresses *extremely* well so you're unlikely to hit the issue unless you deliberately turn off compression. But in general it does make it better. \n\nThe general problem remains though.",
