            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "What we could try for the lengthy compressed string, at least, is to store it as a contiguous C array of short chunks, maybe 16 bytes:\n```c\nconst char cdata[count][16] = { {\"16bytes…\"}, {\"16bytes…\"}, …, {\"16bytes 0-padded\"}};\nconst char* cstring = (const char*) cdata;\n```\nI chose 16 bytes because it should avoid overly long padding sequences at the end. Storing the chunks as array prevents the NUL characters at the end of the C strings and should thus result in the original contiguous string in memory, with a bit of padding at the end.",
